From db76025bff9d35f29c5370ed29ae5ad7231d1dae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Parker Nolan <parker.k.nolan@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:37:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Add Immortal Snail Chess variants
 (snail-{2,3,4}-{d,s}-{u,w})

Two uncapturable snails (custom piece 'S'/'s') step one square toward the
enemy king every 2, 3 or 4 full moves and crush what they land on.
Variants differ in step interval, movement (diagonal or rook steps) and
strength (unstoppable, or weak: only the hunted king can be crushed and
other pieces are walked around). The tick runs inside do_move/undo_move,
the hash includes the tick phase, and crushed kings or a king exposed by a
snail end the game. tests/snail/compare.py checks the fork against the
game's TypeScript engine, which is the reference.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014fb7yruAJNCSruyqMn1GUe
